.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt SCT_VALIDATE 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm SCT_validate ,
.Nm SCT_LIST_validate ,
.Nm SCT_get_validation_status
.Nd checks Signed Certificate Timestamps (SCTs) are valid
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/ct.h
.Ft typedef enum {
     SCT_VALIDATION_STATUS_NOT_SET,
     SCT_VALIDATION_STATUS_UNKNOWN_LOG,
     SCT_VALIDATION_STATUS_VALID,
     SCT_VALIDATION_STATUS_INVALID,
     SCT_VALIDATION_STATUS_UNVERIFIED,
     SCT_VALIDATION_STATUS_UNKNOWN_VERSION
 } sct_validation_status_t;

 int
.Fo SCT_validate
.Fa "SCT *sct"
.Fa "const CT_POLICY_EVAL_CTX *ctx"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo SCT_LIST_validate
.Fa "const STACK_OF(SCT) *scts"
.Fa "CT_POLICY_EVAL_CTX *ctx"
.Fc
.Ft sct_validation_status_t
.Fo SCT_get_validation_status
.Fa "const SCT *sct"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn SCT_validate
will check that an SCT is valid and verify its signature.
.Fn SCT_LIST_validate
performs the same checks on an entire stack of SCTs.
The result of the validation checks can be obtained by passing the SCT
to
.Fn SCT_get_validation_status .
.Pp
A CT_POLICY_EVAL_CTX must be provided that specifies:
.Bl -bullet
.It
The certificate the SCT was issued for.
.Pp
Failure to provide the certificate will result in the validation status
being SCT_VALIDATION_STATUS_UNVERIFIED.
.It
The issuer of that certificate.
.Pp
This is only required if the SCT was issued for a pre-certificate (see
RFC 6962). If it is required but not provided, the validation status
will be SCT_VALIDATION_STATUS_UNVERIFIED.
.It
A CTLOG_STORE that contains the CT log that issued this SCT.
.Pp
If the SCT was issued by a log that is not in this CTLOG_STORE, the
validation status will be SCT_VALIDATION_STATUS_UNKNOWN_LOG.
.El
.Pp
If the SCT is of an unsupported version (only v1 is currently
supported), the validation status will be
SCT_VALIDATION_STATUS_UNKNOWN_VERSION.
.Pp
If the SCT's signature is incorrect, its timestamp is in the future
(relative to the time in CT_POLICY_EVAL_CTX), or if it is otherwise
invalid, the validation status will be SCT_VALIDATION_STATUS_INVALID.
.Pp
If all checks pass, the validation status will be
SCT_VALIDATION_STATUS_VALID.
.Sh NOTES
A return value of 0 from
.Fn SCT_LIST_validate
should not be interpreted as a failure.
At a minimum, only one valid SCT may provide sufficient confidence that
a certificate has been publicly logged.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn SCT_validate
returns a negative integer if an internal error occurs, 0 if the SCT
fails validation, or 1 if the SCT passes validation.
.Pp
.Fn SCT_LIST_validate
returns a negative integer if an internal error occurs, 0 if any of SCTs
fails validation, or 1 if they all pass validation.
.Pp
.Fn SCT_get_validation_status
returns the validation status of the SCT. If
.Fn SCT_validate
or
.Fn SCT_LIST_validate
have not been passed that SCT, the returned value will be
SCT_VALIDATION_STATUS_NOT_SET.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ct 7
.Sh HISTORY
These functions were added in OpenSSL 1.1.0.
